# WAITS ON: whether the Bestiary's metamod recipe can craft a partial
# protection, "1 Suffix Modifier cannot be changed" among them (QUESTIONS.md
# Q128). The checker reads that it can, so the recipe no longer proves the lock.
#
# The Wild Bristle Matron trick: a random metamod made deterministic.
#
# The Bestiary recipe adds one of the five metamods at random, among those
# that fit. Four of them are suffixes; only "Suffixes Cannot Be Changed" is a
# prefix. Fill the suffixes first and the recipe has one choice left, so the
# checker proves which metamod the item carries and the Harvest reforge that
# follows is known to keep the suffixes. Each round needs a prefix slot for the
# metamod; when the reforge fills the prefixes, an Eldritch Orb of Annulment
# under the Exarch's dominance opens one without touching the suffixes.

item {
    base:     "Titan Greaves"
    ilvl:     86
    rarity:   rare
    prefixes: [ "maximum life" t1 ]
    suffixes: [ "fire resistance" t1, "cold resistance" t1, "chaos resistance" t2 ]
}

ember lesser

until has "movement speed" t1 and has "maximum life" t1 {
    if prefixCount == 3 {
        eldritch annul
    }
    beast metamod
    harvest reforge "speed"
}
